Feature: SQL Logic for f_invntry_bal_dly_hist Table Construction

Background:
  Given tables are in the schema purgo_playground
  And the data needs to be sourced from multiple tables with specific join conditions

Scenario Outline: Construct daily inventory balance history with valid data
  Given the item quantity is sourced from purgo_playground.item_qty_on_hand
  And the item ledger entries are sourced from purgo_playground.itemledgerentrieswopd with latest posting_date records
  And reservation entries are filtered with reservation_status = '0' and source_type='37'
  And join purgo_playground.itemledgerentrieswopd on item_no_ and location_code
  And concatenate the source_system_cd and <column_names> for unique keys
  When mapping fields according to the provided Excel sheet definitions
  Then construct the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table with the following fields and logic:

    | Target Field                | Mapping Logic                                                                                             |
    |-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
    | co_key                      | Concatenate source_system_cd and g_company_cd                                                             |
    | g_account                   | Map from sap_master_data profit_center                                                                    |
    | g_assignment_type           | Hardcoded to 'Account'                                                                                    |
    | g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd       | Current system date                                                                                      |
    | g_company_cd                | Hardcoded to '1050'                                                                                       |
    | g_company_currency_cd       | Hardcoded to 'EUR'                                                                                        |
    | g_dnsa_dt_yyyymmdd          | Map from itemledgerentrieswopd.Expiration_Date                                                            |
    | g_expiration_dt_yyyymmdd    | Default value '99991231' if not represented, else from itemledgerentrieswopd.Expiration_Date               |
    | g_item_nbr                  | Map from itemledgerentrieswopd.Item_No_                                                                   |
    | g_location_cd               | Map from itemledgerentrieswopd.Location_Code                                                              |
    | g_location_status_cd        | Hardcoded to 'none'                                                                                     |
    | g_lot_effective_dt_yyyymmdd | Map from itemledgerentrieswopd.Posting_Date                                                               |
    | g_lot_nbr                   | Map from itemledgerentrieswopd.serial_no_, lot_no_, default 'none' if blank                               |
    | g_lot_status_cd             | Hardcoded to 'none'                                                                                     |
    | g_plant_cd                  | Hardcoded to 'CAGER'                                                                                     |
    | g_qty_allocated             | Logic described in Excel sheet notes, and sourced from reservation_entry quantity_base                     |
    | g_qty_available             | Logic described in Excel sheet notes, and sourced from item_qty_on_hand.qty_on_hand                       |
    | g_qty_financial_nettable    | Logic described in Excel sheet notes, and sourced from item_qty_on_hand.qty_on_hand                       |
    | g_qty_in_transit            | Hardcoded to NULL                                                                                        |
    | g_qty_mrp_nettable          | Logic described in Excel sheet notes, and sourced from item_qty_on_hand.qty_on_hand                       |
    | g_qty_on_hand               | Map from item_qty_on_hand.qty_on_hand                                                                    |
    | g_qty_shippable             | Logic described in Excel sheet notes, and sourced from item_qty_on_hand.qty_on_hand                       |
    | g_source_system_cd          | Hardcoded to 'nav_ger'                                                                                   |
    | g_unit_cost_company_currency| Map from Itemwopd.Standard_Cost                                                                          |
    | plant_key                   | Concatenate source_system_cd and g_plant_cd                                                               |
    | plant_location_key          | Concatenate source_system_cd, g_plant_cd, g_location_cd                                                   |
    | prod_key                    | Concatenate source_system_cd, g_item_nbr                                                                  |
    | prod_plant_key              | Concatenate source_system_cd, g_item_nbr, g_plant_cd                                                      |
    | prod_plant_location_key     | Concatenate source_system_cd, g_item_nbr, g_plant_cd, g_location_cd                                       |
    | prod_plant_lot_key          | Concatenate source_system_cd, g_item_nbr, g_plant_cd, g_lot_nbr                                           |
    | prod_plant_lot_location_key | Concatenate source_system_cd, g_item_nbr, g_plant_cd, g_lot_nbr, g_location_cd                            |

  Examples:
    | column_names                  |
    | g_company_cd                  |
    | g_plant_cd                    |
    | g_item_nbr                    |

Scenario: Handle error scenarios in data mapping
  Given incomplete data fields or incorrect values in source tables
  When validating data quality and completeness according to rules
  Then report error message "Data validation failed: Missing or incorrect values in source data."
